 tokens (`"/a~1b/0"` gives `["a/b", "0"]`). See [ADR 0001](docs/adr/0001-json-pointer.md) for the
 design decisions.
+
+### JSON Patch (RFC 6902)
+
+`applyPatch(document, patch)` applies a JSON Patch, an array of operations, to `document` and returns
+the result as a new value. Neither argument is mutated, and the result shares no object or array with
+them.
+
+```ts
+import { applyPatch } from "json-toolkit";
+
+applyPatch({ foo: "bar", list: [1] }, [
+  { op: "add", path: "/baz", value: "qux" }, // add or overwrite a member, insert an array element
+  { op: "add", path: "/list/-", value: 2 }, // "-" appends to an array
+  { op: "replace", path: "/foo", value: "boo" }, // the target must exist
+  { op: "remove", path: "/baz" }, // the target must exist
+  { op: "copy", from: "/list", path: "/copy" },
+  { op: "move", from: "/copy", path: "/moved" }, // not into its own descendant
+  { op: "test", path: "/moved", value: [1, 2] }, // fails unless the values are equal
+]); // { foo: "boo", list: [1, 2], moved: [1, 2] }
+```
+
+The operations are applied in order, each to the result of the previous one. Paths are JSON Pointers
+(see above), and a `path` of `""` addresses the whole document (`remove` cannot remove it). `test`
+compares JSON values structurally: objects have the same members in any order, arrays the same
+elements in the same order, and `1` never equals `"1"`. Members of an operation other than its own are
+ignored.
+
+It throws a `JsonPatchError` (whose `index` and `operation` properties identify the failing operation,
+and whose `cause` holds the underlying error, such as a `JsonPointerError`) when:
+
+- the patch is invalid: not an array, an operation that is not an object, an unknown `op`, a missing
+  or invalid `path` or `from`, a missing `value` for `add`, `replace` or `test`, or a `value` that is
+  not JSON (only `null`, booleans, finite numbers, strings, arrays and plain objects are);
+- the document is not a JSON value (then `index` is `undefined`, like for a patch that is not an
+  array);
+- an operation fails: its target or its `from` does not exist, it adds to a nonexistent parent or at
+  an out-of-range index, it moves a value into itself, or a `test` does not match.
+
+The whole patch is validated before any operation runs, and on failure nothing is returned: a patch
+applies completely or not at all. See [ADR 0002](docs/adr/0002-json-patch.md) for the design decisions.
